{"id":"seuclidean_distance","title":"Standardized Euclidean","family":"lock-step","definition":"reference","intro_en":"Standardized Euclidean distance divides each squared coordinate residual by a supplied variance. Coordinates with greater reference variation receive less weight. This animation uses an explicit, fixed variance vector, so the comparison does not secretly estimate scale from the two sequences being scored. The final root gives a distance in variance-standardized coordinates.","intro_zh":"标准化欧氏距离用给定方差缩放每个坐标的平方残差。参考变化更大的坐标权重较低。本动图使用显式固定的方差向量，不从待比较的两条序列暗中估计尺度，最后开平方得到标准化坐标空间中的距离。","steps_en":["Align samples and provide a positive reference variance for every coordinate.","Square each residual and divide it by that coordinate's variance.","Sum the standardized squared contributions.","Take the square root; retain the same variance vector for future comparisons."],"steps_zh":["对齐采样点，为每个坐标提供正的参考方差。","平方残差后除以对应坐标的方差。","累加标准化平方项。","开平方；后续比较保持同一参考方差。"],"formula":"sqrt(sum_i (x_i-y_i)^2 / v_i), with fixed v_i > 0","caveats_en":["Zero variances need an explicit exclusion or regularization policy.","Estimating variances using test data can leak information; use a declared reference fit."],"caveats_zh":["零方差需要明确的剔除或正则化策略。","用测试数据估计方差可能泄漏信息；应声明参考拟合来源。"],"sources":[{"label":"SciPy: seuclidean","url":"https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.spatial.distance.seuclidean.html"}],"x":[1.0,1.5,2.4,3.7,4.5,3.8,2.6,2.1,2.8,3.8,4.1,3.3],"y":[1.3,1.8,2.0,3.2,5.2,4.4,2.9,1.6,2.6,3.1,4.4,3.9],"input_label":"Deterministic synthetic illustration; sample index is the time axis.","parameters":{"variance":[0.4,0.6,1.0,1.5,2.0,1.3,0.9,0.7,1.1,1.7,1.8,1.2],"variance_source":"fixed illustrative vector"},"result":{"label":"distance","value":1.5347089402273921,"detail":""},"frames":[{"phase":0,"caption":"Aligned samples","panel":{"kind":"lines","title":"Aligned samples","a":[1.0,1.5],"a_label":"x","b":[1.3,1.8],"b_label":"y","marker":1}},{"phase":0,"caption":"Aligned s